# Job Plot Artifacts And Caching

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

## User-facing contract

- The SPA still receives Bokeh **`json_item`** payloads (`plot_item` in JSON). Do not change that shape unless the React embed path is updated in the same task.

## Layers (read order)

1. **Redis (L1)** — keys managed like `JOB_PLOTS_*` in `hpcperfstats/site/lib/machine/api.py`. Very large payloads may be skipped or capped; see **`JOB_PLOT_REDIS_MAX_BYTES`** (default order of ~512 KiB in `job_plot_artifacts.get_job_plot_redis_max_bytes`).
2. **PostgreSQL (L2, durable)** — model **`job_plot_artifact`**: one row per **`(jid, plot_kind, layout)`**. Payload is **gzip-compressed JSON** of the `json_item` dict; encoding constant **`gzip_json`** (`PAYLOAD_ENCODING_GZIP_JSON`).

## Canonical modules

| Concern | Location |
|--------|----------|
| Fingerprint, compress/decompress, upsert, prewarm orchestration | `hpcperfstats/site/lib/machine/job_plot_artifacts.py` |
| Plot kinds / builders | `JOB_PLOT_KINDS` → `hpcperfstats/analysis/metrics/lib/plot` helpers |
| Zoom layout on models / JSON | `hpcperfstats/site/lib/machine/bokeh_plot_layout.py` |
| HTTP assembly + Redis | `job_plots` in `hpcperfstats/site/lib/machine/api.py` |
| Prewarm after metrics | `hpcperfstats/analysis/metrics/update_metrics.py` → `persist_job_plot_artifacts_for_jid` |
| Invalidate Redis **and** DB rows | `invalidate_job_plot_cache_keys_for_jids` in `cache_utils.py` (ingest / sync paths) |

## Fingerprint and schema bumps

- **`compute_plot_input_fingerprint`** hashes job window, host list, `metrics_distinct_time_count`, **live** distinct time count (`LiveDistinctHostTimeCount` on PostgreSQL), `bokeh.__version__`, and **`APP_PLOT_ARTIFACT_SCHEMA_VERSION`**.
- Full Bokeh bump steps (JS + Python pins, CDN test pin, fixtures) live in **`bokeh-version-and-vendor-patch-upgrade.mdc`**.
- When plot **semantics** change without a Bokeh upgrade, bump **`APP_PLOT_ARTIFACT_SCHEMA_VERSION`** in `job_plot_artifacts.py` so old rows are not reused.

## Gaps and boundaries

- **`type_detail`** and similar endpoints are **not** the same code path as `job_plots`; they do not automatically use `job_plot_artifact`. Extend caching there explicitly if those pages are hot.
- Avoid **circular imports** between `api.py` and `update_metrics.py`; shared logic stays in **`job_plot_artifacts`** (and plot modules).

## Tests

- Extend `hpcperfstats/site/lib/machine/tests/test_job_plot_artifacts.py` (and related API tests) when changing persist/load, fingerprint, or invalidation behavior.

## SPA Bokeh embed budget

- **Default:** `deferEmbedUntilVisible` (IntersectionObserver) for every embed unless there is exactly one plot on screen or the embed follows an explicit user gesture (e.g. enlarge dialog).
- **Never** mount N>1 simultaneous Bokeh embeds with `deferEmbedUntilVisible={false}` on list/dashboard surfaces.
- **Global lock:** `BokehEmbed` serializes `embed_item` via `bokehEmbedChain`; lazy-mount heavy sections (pub dashboard year/month toggle, job-list charts tab) to avoid stampeding the lock.
- **List stagger:** pass `embedStaggerIndex` (0, 1, 2, …) on job-list histogram thumbs so embed starts are spaced by `LIST_EMBED_STAGGER_MS` (see `bokeh-embed-defaults.ts`).
- **Unmount:** abort pending embed pipelines on route/view unmount (`AbortController` + early return in lock callback) so list→detail navigation does not wait behind stale embeds.

## Overlap

- Complements **`runtime-resource-and-metrics-safety.mdc`** (metrics recompute) and **`monitor-analysis-architecture-sync.mdc`** (plot inputs from `host_data` / `jid_table`).
- Complements **`interactive-ready-controls.mdc`** (lazy-mount list/dashboard histograms; no embed in hidden tabpanels).
- Complements **`bokeh-version-and-vendor-patch-upgrade.mdc`** when upgrading Bokeh.
- Complements **`update-metrics-job-listing-new-data-type.mdc`** when plot artifacts imply new or changed **`_jobs_queryset`** candidacy.
